# Architecture

- React components should focus on presentation and user interaction.
- Keep API access and reusable business logic in appropriate existing modules.
- Keep FastAPI endpoints thin where business logic can be separated cleanly.
- Validate data at trust boundaries and handle external service failures explicitly.
- Isolate Gemini and LangChain integration details behind clear interfaces when useful.
- Avoid circular dependencies and unnecessary layers.

# Documentation

- Update documentation when setup, behavior, configuration, API contracts, or architecture changes.
- Keep examples and commands consistent with the actual repository.
- Explain why a non-obvious architectural decision exists.
- Do not add comments that merely paraphrase the next line of code.
  